## Cross-PR quality gates (must pass continuously)
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode clean, zero `any` except explicitly documented boundary adapters.
- [ ] Deterministic behavior for tile processing and decoration seeds.
- [ ] Every PR includes perf notes (CPU/GPU/memory delta).
- [ ] Every PR includes debug toggles for the new subsystem.
- [ ] Every PR includes failure-path handling (timeouts, invalid geometry, cache corruption).

## Suggested test matrix
- [ ] Unit: projection, tile math, width resolver, graph builders, cache key/version logic.
- [ ] Property tests: geometry validity (non-zero areas, manifold-ish junction meshes).
- [ ] Integration: fetch->normalize->build->render->dispose for one tile and tile rings.
- [ ] Soak: 20+ min continuous movement without memory growth trend.
- [ ] Offline: cached area available after hard refresh with network disabled.

